{#
    The level is the depth the parser found, and six is as deep as Markdown
    counts. A heading is one line: what an author wrapped over two joins up.

    The section's own anchor stands above it, the page's own title included,
    which is a place references point at too. Otherwise a reader of this file
    has to *derive* one from the words, and every reader derives it
    differently. "The bar's sections" is one apostrophe away from a link that
    lands nowhere.
#}
{%- autoescape false -%}
{%- if node.id %}<a id="{{ node.id }}"></a>

{% endif -%}
{{ '######'|slice(0, min(node.level, 6)) }} {{ renderNode(node.value)|md_line }}

{% endautoescape %}